.TH SCS-CRTMANAGER 1 "September 2026" "sslcrtsrv 0.8.4" "SSLCrtSrv Manual"
.SH NAME
scs-crtmanager \- manage SSLCrtSrv's certificate inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scs-crtmanager
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scs-crtmanager
is a server-side administration tool for the certificate inventory: listing,
adding certificates from existing files, replacing certificate data,
deleting certificates, reporting stale downloads, and managing the
ACME provider assigned to each certificate. Running it with no subcommand at
all prints help and exits 1.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.BI "list " "[\-\-requested] [\-\-clients]"
The certificate inventory.
.B \-\-requested
shows only pending/unissued certificates;
.B \-\-clients
also shows which clients have access to each one.
.TP
.BI "addlocal " "key_file cert_file [intermediate_file]"
Add a certificate from existing PEM files \(em no
.B acme.sh
involved. FQDNs are extracted from the certificate itself.
.TP
.BI "update " "key_file cert_file [intermediate_file]"
Replace an existing certificate's files in place, keeping every reference to
it (client permissions) intact.
.TP
.BI "delete " identifier
Delete a certificate (identified by its FQDNs or database row ID) and its
.B acme.sh
working directory, after an interactive yes/no confirmation.
.TP
.B delete-invalid
List, then (after confirmation) bulk-delete, every expired certificate.
.TP
.BI "warn-stale-downloads " "[\-\-days N]"
Per-client report of active certificate assignments whose last
.I downloaded
copy is expiring within
.I N
days (default 21), already superseded by a renewal, or never downloaded at
all.
.TP
.BI "set-provider " "identifier provider"
Change which ACME provider a certificate uses, or set it to
.B manual
to permanently exclude it from
.BR scs-crtrequest (1) 's
automation.
.TP
.BI "init-db-key " "[\-\-overwrite]"
One-time: generate the at-rest database-encryption keypair.
.B \-\-overwrite
is dangerous \(em it orphans every already-encrypted row unless re-encrypted
first.
.TP
.BI "migrate-encrypt-keys " "[\-\-dry-run]"
One-time: encrypt any legacy plaintext private keys already in the database.
.SH FILES
.I /etc/sslcrtsrv/server_config.json
\(em read for the database location and certificate directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scs-server (1),
.BR scs-cltmanager (1),
.BR scs-admintui (1),
.BR scs-crtrequest (1)
.PP
The project's
.I Manual.MD
has the full narrative reference.
